Iska Seedha Matlab Kya Hai?

Ye property yeh batati hai ki: TimeoutNotification node kis mode me kaam karega — Automatic ya Controlled?


---

Do Modes Hote Hain:

1. Automatic Mode:

Node kisi bhi TimeoutControl node ke paired nahi hota.

Matlab: Ye khud hi independent timeout request generate karta hai.

Jo bhi timeout interval hoga, wo "Timeout Value" property ke basis pe hoga (tumhe manually ek positive number dena hoga, e.g., 60 seconds).


Example: Soch le ki tumhara app har 60 second baad kuch check karna chahta hai — to tu TimeoutNotification node ko Automatic pe set karega aur Timeout Value me 60 daalega. Ab ye node har 60 second me khud hi fire hoga, bina kisi control ke.


---

2. Controlled Mode:

Is mode me ye node kisi TimeoutControl node ke saath paired hota hai.

Ye khud timeout request generate nahi karta.

Ye sirf un timeout requests ko process karta hai jo TimeoutControl node ne pahle store kiya tha.


Example: Soch le kisi user ne "Remind me after 10 mins" ka request dala. Ye request TimeoutControl node store karta hai. Jab 10 mins ho jaate hain, tab TimeoutNotification node (in Controlled mode) us request ko process karta hai.


---

Ek Line Me Difference:

Mode	Kya Karta Hai TimeoutNotification Node?

Automatic	Khud se timeout request generate karta hai
Controlled	Paired TimeoutControl node ke stored timeout requests ko process karta hai



---

Real-life Analogy:

Automatic Mode: Alarm clock jo har 60 mins me baja raha hai, bina kisi instruction ke.

Controlled Mode: Reminder app jo tabhi bajta hai jab tumne pehle se koi specific reminder set kiya ho.



