---

Yeh Property Kya Karti Hai?

> “The interval (in seconds) between timeout requests.”



Iska matlab:

Jab tumhara TimeoutNotification node Automatic mode me hota hai, to yeh property decide karti hai ki kitne second ke baad ek new timeout request generate hogi.



---

Example:

Agar tu Timeout Interval = 30 set karta hai, to node har 30 second me ek timeout request generate karega.

Jaise: 0 sec, 30 sec, 60 sec, 90 sec, ...



---

Important Note:

> “If the Operation Mode is set to Automatic, the value of the Timeout Interval property is overridden by the Timeout interval property, if set, in the Timer configurable service.”



Yani:

Agar tumne integration server me Timer configurable service me bhi ek timeout interval set kiya hai,

To wo value yahan wali Timeout Interval value ko override (replace) kar degi.



---

Simple Table to Samajhne ke Liye:

Scenario	Final Timeout Interval (in seconds)

Operation Mode = Controlled	Irrelevant — property ka koi effect nahi
Operation Mode = Automatic, Timer service not set	Use Timeout Interval value from node
Operation Mode = Automatic, Timer service is set	Use value from Timer configurable service (overrides node value)



---

Real-life Analogy:

Soch le tu ek timer laga raha hai:

Agar tu manually 60 seconds set karta hai (node ka property),

Lekin kitchen me already ek default timer 30 seconds ka set hai (Timer service),

To kitchen ka timer tumhara set kiya hua override kar dega.



---

Final Points:

Ye property tabhi kaam karti hai jab Operation Mode = Automatic ho.

Value hamesha positive integer honi chahiye.

Agar Timer service configured hai, to wahi interval use hoga.



