Yeh node mostly timer-based flows ke liye use hoti hai, jahan tu chahta hai ki kuch kaam ek specific time ya interval pe ho — jaise:

Har 5 minute me report generate karna

Raat 12 baje batch process run karna

Hourly currency rates fetch karna



---

TimeoutNotification Node ke Do Use Cases:

1. Paired with TimeoutControl node (Controlled Mode):

TimeoutControl node ek "timeout request" bhejta hai (jaise: “yeh kaam 10 min baad karna”)

TimeoutNotification node us request ko receive karke, jab time pura ho jata hai, tab message propagate karta hai next node ko.

Matlab: Tum manually control kar rahe ho ki notification kab aaye.


Important:
Dono nodes (Control & Notification) ke Unique Identifier same hone chahiye, warna pairing nahi hogi.


---

2. Standalone Mode (Automatic Mode):

Koi TimeoutControl nahi hota, yeh node khud hi periodic message generate karta hai.

Tum config me set karte ho: “Har 60 seconds me ek message bhejna hai”

Yeh automation mode me hota hai aur config me set interval ke according flow trigger karta hai.



---

Important Properties:

Unique Identifier: Yeh name hota hai jisse pairing hoti hai control aur notification node ki.

IgnoreMissed: Agar message miss ho gaya (broker down tha), to uska kya kare — ignore kare ya process.

Timer Configurable Service: Agar default timeout queue (SYSTEM.BROKER.TIMEOUT.QUEUE) nahi chahiye to custom queue specify karne ke liye use hota hai.

MQMD (Message Queue Descriptor): Agar output WebSphere MQ pe bhejna hai to proper MQMD dena padta hai (warna error aayega).



---

Jab Broker Start Hota Hai:

Node check karta hai internal timeout store me koi pending request hai kya.

Agar koi persistent request hai (missed ho gayi) aur IgnoreMissed = False hai to wo notification fir bhi trigger karega.



---

Use Case Example:

Scenario: Tujhe chahiye ki har raat 12 baje ek salary processing batch chale:

Use TimeoutControl node to set “Midnight Trigger”

Use TimeoutNotification node to receive that trigger and start flow

Flow jaake database me salary update kare, log file me likhe, email bheje etc.



---

In Short Summary:

Feature	Controlled Mode (With TimeoutControl)	Automatic Mode (Stand-alone)

Who triggers?	TimeoutControl node	Self-trigger based on config
Flexibility	High (custom timing per request)	Fixed periodic trigger
Use Case	Specific, per-user timeout	Regular batch jobs
Needs MQMD?	Only if not already present	Yes



